<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Elands Q1 available profit falls.</title>
<headline>Elands Q1 available profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-March versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Available profit			  31.1 vs 41.3</p>
<p>    Capital spending			  13.4 vs 25.0</p>
<p>    Gold output (kg)			 3,939 vs 4,242</p>
<p>    Tonnes milled/treated		536,000 vs 552,000</p>
<p>    Yield (gram/t)			    7.20 vs 7.60</p>
<p>    Cost (rand/kg)			  38,053 vs 36,136</p>
<p>    Revenue (rand/kg)		     53,020 vs 55,800</p>
<p>Full name: Elandsrand Gold Mining Co Ltd, managed by Anglo American Corp of South Africa Ltd.</p>
<p>NOTE - The mine is on track to achieve forecast gold output of 16 tonnes in 1997.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
